# Token efficiency

Prefer finishing the ask with the smallest useful context. This rule is short on purpose — do not expand it.

## Search before reading

- Use `Grep` / `Glob` first; open only the few matching files.
- Prefer `Read` with `offset`/`limit` on large files (e.g. `AppShell.jsx`). Do not dump whole controllers, services, or migrations.
- Do not re-read a file already returned in this turn unless it changed.

## No speculative exploration

- Skip explore/subagents for narrow edits, single-symbol lookups, or 1–3 known files.
- Do not crawl the whole backend/frontend when the path is already clear.

## Implement tightly

- Change only what the task needs. Prefer targeted edits over rewriting whole files.
- No docs, README, comments, refactors, or drive-by cleanup unless asked.
- Do not run broad builds, full test suites, or migrators unless required to verify this change or the user asked.

## Responses

- Answer in a few short sentences or bullets. Cite only the lines that matter.
